      "signpost": "reflexive",
      "definition": "used as the object of a verb or preposition when the action affects a man, boy, or male animal already mentioned, the same one who is the subject",
      "explanation": "**Himself** is used when the subject and the object of the same clause refer to the same male person or animal: *he cut himself*. It is not just another way of saying **him**: use **him** when the object is a different person from the subject, *give it to him*, not *give it to himself*.",
